# 0.7.5 - MM-LIFE-2h, the array form's length. It was read out of the
# allocator's word count in bits 1..14 of the shape word, and that is a
# SIZE CLASS the allocator clamps to 0 past 16,383 words: a container's
# element buffer of 131,072 bytes or more announced itself as an array
# of zero handles and the release walk reclaimed none of its elements.
# The length moves to bits 16..62, and nothing could recover a number
# the allocator had already thrown away - so the marker takes the count
# from its caller, all four of which already had it in scope. See
# docs/memory-model.md MM-LIFE-2h and
# tests/stdlib/406-array-form-large-block.ax.
0.7.5  F  memMarkArray  (-> Int Int) -> (-> Int Int Int): the array form carries its own length
